==English==

===Etymology===
First coined to serve as an {{l|en|antonym}} of {{m|en|entropy}}, substituting its {{m|en||en-}} element (representing the prepositional prefix {{m|grc|ἐν}}, ''en'', “in” in its {{uder|en|grc|-}} etymon {{m|grc|ἐντροπία}}, ''entropia'', “a turning towards”) with {{m|en||ex-}} (representing the {{uder|en|grc|ἐξ}}, ''ex'', “out of”, “from”); because {{m|grc||ἐξ}} takes the form {{m|grc|ἐκ}} when prefixed to an element beginning with {{m|grc|τ}}, the analogical spelling is {{m|en|ectropy}} (or, alternatively, {{m|en|ektropy}}), as if after the {{uder|en|grc|-}} *{{m|grc||ἐκτροπία|a turning out of}}.

